
### Description

    The testbench is used for testing arbiter driver. It can config arbiter
params(enable, time window) and masters params(enable, urgent, bw_overflow
and weight). In addition, irq status can aslo be checked.

### USAGE

> make clean all
> ./arbiter_test [option]

    Before using the testbench, you should load arbiter driver firstly. The option
is defined in arbiter_get_option.h. If you want config any arbiter, you must specify
the arbiter id in option; if you want config any master of arbiter, you must sepcify
the arbiter id and master id in option.

#### Example

1. if config arbiter[0]
> ./arbiter_test --arbId=0 --arbEnable=1 --timeWindow=29

2. if config master[0] of arbiter[0]
> ./arbiter_test --arbId=0 --masterId=0 --onLine=1 --urgent=1 --weight=31 --bwOverflow=0

3. check irq status:
  1) if waitTimeout=0, will keep waiting any arbiter err irq with wait_event_interruptible;
  2) if waitTimeout!=0, will wait any arbiter err irq with wait_event_interruptible_timeout,
       if not waited, then will timeout after waitTimeout ms.

> ./arbiter_test --checkIrq=1 --waitTimeout=0

